  "lines": [
    {
      "text": "In twenty ten, Xavi and Iniesta won everything, and lost the Ballon d'Or to their own teammate.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "title",
        "heading": "XAVI & INIESTA",
        "sub": "Barcelona & Spain · 2010",
        "pill": "ROBBED BY A TEAMMATE?",
        "person": "iniesta"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "First, Barcelona won the league with ninety-nine points. A Spanish record back then.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "stats",
        "title": "La Liga 2009/10",
        "items": [
          {
            "n": "99",
            "l": "points"
          },
          {
            "n": "1",
            "l": "league title"
          }
        ],
        "person": "xavi"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Then South Africa. Xavi completed more passes than anyone at the World Cup.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "person",
        "person": "xavi",
        "label": "Most completed passes, World Cup 2010",
        "mood": "happy"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "And Iniesta? The hundred and sixteenth minute of the final.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "score",
        "home": "ned",
        "away": "esp",
        "hs": 0,
        "as": 1,
        "date": "11 July 2010",
        "comp": "World Cup final",
        "note": "Iniesta 116'"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Spain, champions of the world for the first time.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "trophies",
        "items": [
          {
            "kind": "worldcup",
            "label": "World Cup 2010"
          },
          {
            "kind": "league",
            "label": "La Liga 2009/10"
          }
        ],
        "person": "iniesta"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Messi's summer? Argentina lost four-nil to Germany. He didn't score a single World Cup goal.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "score",
        "home": "arg",
        "away": "ger",
        "hs": 0,
        "as": 4,
        "date": "3 July 2010",
        "comp": "World Cup quarter-final"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "But his club season was mad. Forty-seven goals, the Pichichi and the Golden Shoe.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "stats",
        "title": "Messi 2009/10",
        "items": [
          {
            "n": "47",
            "l": "goals, all comps"
          },
          {
            "n": "34",
            "l": "league goals"
          }
        ],
        "person": "messi"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "And when the votes came in, Messi first. Iniesta second. Xavi third.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "podium",
        "year": "2010",
        "title": "FIFA Ballon d'Or",
        "places": [
          {
            "person": "messi",
            "club": "bar"
          },
          {
            "person": "iniesta",
            "club": "esp"
          },
          {
            "person": "xavi",
            "club": "esp"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Twenty-two point six percent for Messi. Seventeen point four for Iniesta. Sixteen point five for Xavi.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "list",
        "title": "FIFA Ballon d'Or 2010",
        "rows": [
          {
            "name": "Lionel Messi",
            "value": "22.65%",
            "club": "bar"
          },
          {
            "name": "Andrés Iniesta",
            "value": "17.36%",
            "club": "bar",
            "hl": true
          },
          {
            "name": "Xavi",
            "value": "16.48%",
            "club": "bar",
            "hl": true
          },
          {
            "name": "Wesley Sneijder",
            "value": "14.48%"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Did the two Spaniards just split the vote?",
      "scene": {
        "type": "versus",
        "title": "Same team, same vote",
        "left": {
          "person": "iniesta",
          "label": "Iniesta",
          "value": "17.36%"
        },
        "right": {
          "person": "xavi",
          "label": "Xavi",
          "value": "16.48%"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "In this alternate world, those Spanish votes land on one man. Thirty-three point eight percent. Messi is nowhere near.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "whatif",
        "title": "What if they hadn't split it?",
        "real": {
          "label": "Messi, real world",
          "value": "22.65%"
        },
        "alt": {
          "label": "One Spaniard, imagined",
          "value": "33.84%"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "All three came through Barcelona's academy. One podium, one club, one very awkward dressing room.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "text",
        "heading": "A UNIQUE PODIUM",
        "body": "Messi, Iniesta and Xavi all came through Barcelona's La Masia academy. Barcelona itself calls it a unique Ballon d'Or podium."
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The World Cup heroes stood on the lower steps.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "stamp",
        "text": "ROBBED",
        "person": "xavi",
        "color": "red"
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Follow for more.",
      "scene": {
        "type": "cta"
      }
    }
  ]
